Campaign navigation left the modal open! When clicking `[data-view="campaign"]` inside the more modal, handler calls setView then closeContext, but doesn't close modal. Actually `go-view` action isn't used; modal uses `data-view` directly, handled by global document click handler (rail) which calls setView but doesn't close modal. This is a bug on both desktop and mobile: selecting a view from MAIS modal leaves the backdrop/modal open, blocking interaction. Need fix: in document click handler for `[data-view]`, if the button is inside modal, close modal. Or in modal buttons use `data-action="go-view"` which calls closeContext but not closeModal either; `go-view` also doesn't close modal. Better global handler:
```
document.addEventListener('click', e => {
 const btn = e.target.closest('[data-view]');
 if (!btn) return;
 click(); setView(btn.dataset.view); this.closeModal();
});
```
Need see context around lines 90-99. It currently:
```
if (this.game.contains?...)...
const btn = e.target.closest('[data-view]');
if (!btn) return;
click();
setView(btn.dataset.view);
```
Add `this.closeModal()`. Check closeModal exists and handles when none. This is a real bug fix. Also ensure rail clicks close modal (harmless).

